cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this simulation or build on the experiment, please cite the repository."
title: "Message in the Ripple"
abstract: >-
  A simulation-first study of transient caustic glyphs: a single finite
  mechanical launch imprints a water surface, free gravity-capillary wave
  propagation carries the disturbance to a designed instant t*, and the light
  refracted through the momentarily shaped surface assembles into a chosen
  symbol before dispersing. Includes a differentiable forward model
  (linear gravity-capillary waves + Snell refraction with bilinear splatting),
  a three-stage inverse design (static caustic design, time reversal,
  constrained launch optimization), and a plan for a physical rig.
authors:
  - family-names: "JD"
    given-names: "Benito"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/BenitoJD/message-in-the-ripple"
keywords:
  - caustics
  - water waves
  - inverse design
  - differentiable simulation
  - time reversal
